meaning:
Bas is claiming that Dreamville has overtaken all its direct opponents, probably including TDE, the independent label owned by Anthony “Top Dawg” Tiffith and mostly known thanks to Kendrick Lamar, by being more active and innovative during that last couple of years.

Let’s see if the New York-based rapper’s statement is credible by taking a look to the amount of works issued between 2018 and the summer of 2019 by the two labels, starting by Dreamville Records:



Effected by Cozz (February 13, 2018);

Royalty by EARTHGANG (February 23, 2018);

KOD by J. Cole (April 20, 2018);

Milky Way by Bas (August 24, 2018);

DiCaprio 2 by JID (November 26, 2018);

Shea Butter Baby by Ari Lennox (May 7, 2019);

Revenge of the Dreamers III (July 5, 2019 – Anticipated by this single).



Bas' compilation Spilled Milk and EARTHGANG’s debut album Mirrorland were on the way to their release, at the time.

Total: 7 works, plus 2 teased ones.

What about Top Dawg?



November by SiR (January 19, 2018);

Black Panther: The Album (Music from and Inspired By), cured by Kendrick Lamar and Anthony Tiffith (February 9, 2018);

Redemption by Jay Rock (June 15, 2018);

Run Wild, Run Free EP by Zacari (March 15, 2019);

CrasH Talk by ScHoolboy Q (April 26, 2019);



SiR’s album Chasing Summer was on the way to its release, at the time.

Total: 5 works, plus one teased LP.

The “rivalry” between Dreamville and TDE was previously discussed by JID, who assumed the need to “up their game” in the face of Top Dawg Entertainment’s success.

Dreamville’s spiritual leader, J. Cole, also talked about this competition, which motivated his label “one hundred percent.”

Some people may have taken Bas' phrase as a jab to TDE members, but the competition between them and Dreamville’s affiliates is absolutely constructive, as the features on some of the previously mentioned records prove: Cole took part in Jay Rock’s “OSOM”; Kendrick Lamar made an appearance on Cozz’s “Hustla’s Story” and did the chorus of “Under The Sun,” featured on ROTD3; finally, on this last compilation, the song “LamboTruck” features Cozz (a Dreamville signee) and REASON (a Top Dawg signee) exchanging some opinions on their labels' working ethic and their satisfaction with it…
